---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import LegalDraft from '../components/LegalDraft.astro';
import { site } from '../lib/data';
const L = site.legal;
---
<Base title="Privacy" description={`Privacy notice for ${site.name}.`} nav="about">
  <section class="band"><div class="page-text">
    <header class="page-head"><h1>Privacy notice</h1>
    <p class="lede">Short version: no cookies, no tracking, no analytics, no third-party resources. Your reading progress stays in your own browser.</p></header>
    <div class="prose">
    <LegalDraft />

    <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
    <p>{L.name}, {L.address}. Email: {L.email}</p>

    <h2>Hosting</h2>
    <p>This site is a static website hosted on GitHub Pages, a service of GitHub, Inc. When you open a page, your browser sends technical data to GitHub's servers, including your IP address, the requested page, time, browser type and referrer. GitHub processes this data to deliver the site and keep it secure, and may store it in server logs. The legal basis is our legitimate interest in providing a reliable, secure website (Art. 6 (1) (f) GDPR). Data may be processed in the United States. Details: <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">GitHub Privacy Statement</a>.</p>

    <h2>Fonts and other resources</h2>
    <p>All fonts, scripts and styles are served from this site itself. No content is loaded from third-party servers, so opening a page does not transmit your IP address to anyone other than the host.</p>

    <h2>Data stored in your browser</h2>
    <p>The site uses your browser's local storage to remember your reading path (beginner or engineer), which checkpoint questions you have answered, and the date of your last visit, so it can highlight what changed. This data never leaves your device and is not sent to us or anyone else. You can delete it at any time by clearing this site's data in your browser, or with "Reset my quiz progress" on the <a href="../about/">How it works</a> page. Because this storage is strictly necessary for features you use, no consent banner is required (§ 25 (2) No. 2 TDDDG).</p>

    <h2>Contact by email</h2>
    <p>If you email us, we use your message and address only to reply, and delete them when they are no longer needed.</p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>Under the GDPR you have the right to access, rectification, erasure, restriction of processing, data portability and objection (Art. 15–21 GDPR). You also have the right to lodge a complaint with a supervisory authority, for example {L.supervisory_authority}.</p>
  </div></div></section>
</Base>
